# Network phase N3: automatic address (DHCP), names (DNS), settings that survive a reboot.
# QEMU's built-in DHCP server gives 10.0.2.15/24, gateway 10.0.2.2, DNS 10.0.2.3.
@net
@disk
@dns bee.test=10.0.2.2 far.test=93.184.216.34
$ net dhcp
~ ^asking the network for an address \(DHCP\) \(saved\)\.\.\.$
address 10.0.2.15/24 (DHCP), gateway 10.0.2.2, DNS 10.0.2.3
$ net
~ ^address: 10\.0\.2\.15/24 \(DHCP, lease ends in [\dhms ]+\)$
gateway: 10.0.2.2
dns:     10.0.2.3
$ cat /system/net
dhcp
$ ping -c 1 10.0.2.2
1 sent, 1 received, 0% loss
# Names: use the test's DNS server.
$ net dns {dns}
~ ^DNS server 10\.0\.2\.2:\d+ \(saved\)$
!~ \[net\]
$ nslookup bee.test
bee.test has address 10.0.2.2
$ nslookup BEE.Test.
BEE.Test. has address 10.0.2.2
$ host far.test
far.test has address 93.184.216.34
$ ping -c 1 bee.test
PING bee.test (10.0.2.2): 32 data bytes
~ ^32 bytes from 10\.0\.2\.2: seq=1
1 sent, 1 received, 0% loss
$ nslookup 10.0.2.2
10.0.2.2 has address 10.0.2.2
$ nslookup nope.test
nope.test: no such name
$ ping nope.test
nope.test: no such name
$ nslookup "bad name"
bad name: not a valid host name
# A server that never answers: asked three times, then a clear message (5 s).
$ nslookup drop.test
drop.test: no answer from the DNS server
# The event log records that the network came up, but never host names.
$ log 40
~ "ev":"net","state":"dhcp-bound"
~ "ev":"cmd","cmd":"nslookup","status":"error"
!~ bee\.test|nope\.test|10\.0\.2
@reboot
~ \[net\]  asking the network for an address \(DHCP\)
$ net dhcp
~ ^address 10\.0\.2\.15/24 \(DHCP\), gateway 10\.0\.2\.2, DNS 10\.0\.2\.2:\d+$
$ nslookup bee.test
bee.test has address 10.0.2.2
$ net dns auto
DNS server: the one DHCP gives (saved)
$ net
dns:     10.0.2.3
# Back to a fixed address: DHCP stops, the DNS server from DHCP is gone.
$ net static 10.0.2.20/24 10.0.2.2
address 10.0.2.20/24, gateway 10.0.2.2 (saved)
$ net
address: 10.0.2.20/24 (static)
dns:     none (net dns ADDRESS)
$ nslookup bee.test
bee.test: no DNS server configured (net dns ADDRESS)
$ ping -c 1 10.0.2.2
1 sent, 1 received, 0% loss
